      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why would someone use offsets instead of region names?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 13,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 14,
        "endChar": 7
      },
      "revId": "bfd6e15a0ffd834ad65ae3cfc362c9f7091c07fa",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7af091e4_31c7db77",
        "filename": "util/ap_ro_hash.py",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 14,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-04-23T00:57:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "the thing is that many (all?) FMAP sections have large gaps. For instance the RO_SECTION section of Grunt flash image has 1205 KB of padding (areas filled up with 0x0 or 0xff) out of 2564 KB",
      "parentUuid": "aafff1be_7a876500",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 13,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 14,
        "endChar": 7
      },
      "revId": "bfd6e15a0ffd834ad65ae3cfc362c9f7091c07fa",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "714d5c6d_17d40572",
        "filename": "util/ap_ro_hash.py",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 14,
      "author": {
        "id": 1136059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-04-23T17:29:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "How will these ranges be determined?\n\nI think it\u0027s safer to use section names in the factory scripts, because it\u0027s less likely they\u0027ll change. I\u0027d worry about someone updating the factory firmware and forgetting to update the the ranges.",
      "parentUuid": "7af091e4_31c7db77",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 13,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 14,
        "endChar": 7
      },
      "revId": "bfd6e15a0ffd834ad65ae3cfc362c9f7091c07fa",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "95d38aab_5a18d233",
        "filename": "util/ap_ro_hash.py",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 14,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-04-23T17:41:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "these ranges can be determined by examining coreboot map files.\n\nThis script as presented does allow using fmap area names only.\n\nThe ability to specify ranges will be handy in case we decide to move to partial verification of the RO space by the GSC, with the rest of the RO space verified by the AP.\n\nThat would allow to greatly speed up the check and hence run it on every EC reset.",
      "parentUuid": "714d5c6d_17d40572",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 13,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 14,
        "endChar": 7
      },
      "revId": "bfd6e15a0ffd834ad65ae3cfc362c9f7091c07fa",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "62b2ca4b_9d9f7cbb",
        "filename": "util/ap_ro_hash.py",
        "patchSetId": 1
